CHOIR — Third-Party Notices
===========================

Required by SRS PKG-005: "All training-pipeline code, licences, and datasets
shall be licence-clean for closed-source commercial distribution of the runtime
(no GPL/AGPL contamination of shipped assets or code; permissive-licensed
research code use documented in a NOTICE file)."

This file lists every third-party work redistributed in this package, so that a
consuming application can satisfy its own attribution obligations.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (CMUdict)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used as the built-in pronunciation lexicon (SRS TXT-020), shipped as
`Sources/Choir/Resources/cmudict.lex` in a sorted, tab-separated form derived
from the upstream `cmudict.dict`. Content is unmodified; only the ordering and
field separator differ, to permit memory-mapped binary search.

    Copyright (C) 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon University. All rights reserved.

Licensed under the two-clause BSD licence. The full text is redistributed
alongside the data at `Sources/Choir/Resources/CMUDICT-LICENSE.txt`, satisfying
the licence's requirement that the copyright notice and conditions accompany
redistributions in source form.

Upstream: https://github.com/cmusphinx/cmudict

This licence is attribution-only. It imposes no copyleft obligation and does not
restrict closed-source or commercial distribution, which is what PKG-005
requires and what Guiding Principle 5 means by a licence that cannot "poison a
commercial App Store product".

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IEEE Harvard Sentences
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used as the intelligibility corpus (SRS QUA-004), in
`Sources/Choir/Quality/HarvardSentences.swift`.

From "IEEE Recommended Practice for Speech Quality Measurements", IEEE No. 297
(1969). These phonetically balanced sentence lists have been published and
reproduced in speech-research literature for over fifty years and are used here
as a measurement instrument rather than as creative content.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Everything else
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No other third-party code, data, or model weights are redistributed. Per
PKG-004 the runtime links only Apple frameworks and has zero third-party
runtime dependencies.

Voice model assets do not yet exist. When they do, ML-A-004 requires their
training data to be licence-clean for closed-source commercial synthesis, with
full provenance recorded — and that provenance belongs in this file.
